WEBVTT

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.460
A corpse wearing a military uniform?

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.280
Ain't heard anything about it.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.210
Is he alive?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:12.250
Whether he is or not,

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.240
we can't leave Yuubari until we know 
if Sergeant Tsukishima is alive or not.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.670
There must be some clue left here.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:33.620
There should be some connection between the

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.380
leftover skins used for 
the taxidermy process,

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.350
and the fake tattooed skins.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:50.860
They got it.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.480
Ienaga, don't go outside!

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.820
They'll shoot you!

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.560
I caught a glimpse of a 
soldier's uniform out there.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:00:59.910
I think there's more than one.

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.500
They're here to destroy the 
evidence of the fake skins?

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.010
There may be kibushi berries still 
left in Edogai-kun's house.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.570
They're what you use to do tannin tanning.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.970
We need to get rid of them all.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:32.070
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.900
<b>Episode Fifteen
Let's Talk About the Past</b>

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:03.820
From the look of it, there are 
two or three people inside.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.060
If Sergeant Tsukishima's report is 
right and Sugimoto Saichi is in there,

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.460
don't kill him!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:10.580
He's mine!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.730
If Lt. Tsurumi's men are here,

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:18.200
I guess we should assume Sergeant Tsukishima 
made it out of the tunnels alive.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.260
Yeah.

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.220
There's iron bars on the windows.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.220
If the soldiers outside want to get in,

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.180
they'll have to come in the front door.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:29.770
I'll make sure they decide to do that.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:34.650
He's above us!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.360
Get under the awning!

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.770
We're going in!

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:41.730
Let's bust down the door—

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.450
Get away from the door!

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.370
Don't leave the awning! He'll shoot you!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.020
There are quite a few of them.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:11.770
Go! Go!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.030
The second floor! Take out the 
sniper on the second floor!

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.180
Damn you!

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.060
<i>I can't get out...</i>

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.820
Ushiyama-sama!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:57.230
Move, Ienaga.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:14.250
Die! Die, you stupid shit!

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.550
What, do you want a "thank you"?

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.510
I didn't save you because 
I wanted to, bat man.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:44.030
Where's Hijikata?!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.940
Hijikata!

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:51.490
Sugimoto Saichi!

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:14.420
Stay hidden!

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:17.670
Poke a finger out from behind 
that corner, and he'll shoot it!

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.600
This is our only chance at escape.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.560
Hurry.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.100
Let's go, old man!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.760
Let's split into two groups and flee.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.510
We'll meet up at Ashibetsu.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:46.980
I'll look for Ienaga and Nagakura's group.

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.090
With no way to tell which skins are fake,

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.550
we'll have to meet Nopperabo directly.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:56.390
He'll probably be willing to 
tell his daughter everything.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:01.300
I should've assumed you knew 
that she was his daughter.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.020
For my part, as long as I get a small share,

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.030
I don't care who does what with the gold.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.780
But Asirpa-san is a true Ainu.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:16.120
Is the person who stole their 
gold really her father?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.830
I want to see her find the truth.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:25.000
So for now, we can assume 
we share the same goal?

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:28.460
We'll both do whatever we feel like.

00:07:55.220 --> 00:08:00.140
<b>The Next Day</b>

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:12.570
We should be careful. Try to run 
into as few people as possible.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:17.460
They'll be looking for locals 
who saw us to track us.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:20.270
Look, Sugimoto.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.800
Those are tureptacir.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.230
Woodcock birds.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:27.070
When it's herb-gathering season,

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:29.240
that's when the woodcocks come to this place.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.270
They're digging holes.

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.570
Are they looking for bugs?

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.930
Their long beaks,
 which they use to find food,

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:40.810
are similar to the tools the Ainu 
use to dig up ubayuri roots.

00:08:40.810 --> 00:08:43.620
So we call them "ubayuri-digging birds."

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.240
Are they tasty?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:46.530
The brains are tasty!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.180
Hey, Ogata. No.

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.300
Why?

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.130
We're eating them, right?

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.800
Even if you hit one, the others will flee.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:01.470
Woodcocks don't fly in a straight line, 
so it'll be hard to hit one with that gun.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:06.440
We have a trap that takes advantage 
of the woodcocks' habits.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:10.010
You make a path with branches that 
the woodcocks will want to follow,

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.880
and fill it up with traps.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.440
If we use traps, we can 
get enough for everybody.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:24.960
The traps worked!

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:28.890
But that's probably not enough for everybody.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:33.170
Help me pluck the feathers, Sugimoto.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:38.280
She's upset because she set so 
many traps and only caught two.

00:09:42.100 --> 00:09:43.910
Three of them?

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.940
I wondered where you went.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:50.260
I'm impressed you managed to 
get so many without buckshot.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.730
Wow, he's annoying.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.380
He got mad because Asirpa-san 
said he couldn't do it.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:01.890
And you're jealous 'cause you 
can't hit shit with a gun!

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.350
I am not!

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.170
Dick-sensei, this is woodcock brain.

00:10:13.370 --> 00:10:17.010
Dick-sensei... do you not like brains?

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.020
Is that edible?

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.420
Sugimoto...

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.060
It's hinna, right?

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:25.180
Hinna, hinna!

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.010
No, I'm fine.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:44.030
Now you use all the rest of it, 
including the organs, to make chitatap!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.520
Chitatap! Hell yes!

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:47.540
Chitatap?

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.830
Smack it while saying "chitatap," Dick-sensei.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:54.790
Chitatap? Chitatap...?

00:10:54.790 --> 00:11:09.180
Chitatap. Chitatap. Chitatap.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:04.980
Take over for him, Ogata.

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.220
Everybody has to help make the chitatap.

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:17.150
Asirpa-san, Ogata isn't saying "chitatap"!

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:25.210
Ogata? What's wrong?

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.110
Now, let's eat!

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:31.540
This is ohau made from woodcock chitatap!

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.330
Let's eat!

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.520
It's so good!

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.090
Hinna, hinna!

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:40.380
Yum.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:42.930
Hinna!

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.010
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:51.270
<b>Barato</b>

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:51.270
You there.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.130
Why are you pretending to be an Ainu?

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:55.230
You're Japanese, right?

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.860
<b>Yamamoto Barbershop</b>

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:02.470
An Ainu child with three men...

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.780
I haven't seen anything like that.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:08.160
Wait, that's not the kid
you're talking about?

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:14.500
Hey, Boner. Don't run.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.170
Don't call me "Boner," Tanigaki Nispa!

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:18.960
My name is Cikapasi!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:22.090
I could tell you were following 
us from a distance.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:24.950
I ignored you on the theory 
that you'd give up eventually.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:27.540
Get back to your kotan.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.210
Everybody there must be worried.

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:31.750
My family is dead.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.650
Nobody is waiting for me back at the kotan.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.370
Take me with you.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.460
Why not take him?

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:43.270
The Sirakki Kamuy says it's 
good luck to take him.

00:12:43.270 --> 00:12:45.450
If the three of us pretend to be a family,

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.450
nobody will be suspicious of us.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:48.380
Really?

00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:49.810
We're pretending to be a family?

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:53.050
Th-Then Inkarmat is my big sister.

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.970
But we have different mothers.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:58.650
You love your little brother and 
don't get mad if I grab your boobs,

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:02.380
and we're looking for our dad, 
whom we've never met, together!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.840
I like that. It sounds fun.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.080
And you're my dad's 
little brother, Tanigaki Nispa,

00:13:09.080 --> 00:13:11.850
and Inkarmat likes you,

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:14.810
but you're hiding the fact that 
you're really her brother.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.610
Cikapasi, that's too complicated.

00:13:16.610 --> 00:13:18.010
Let's make it simpler.

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:18.900
Yeah?

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.400
Okay, so Inkarmat is my big sister,

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:24.070
and she doesn't get mad at 
<i>all</i> if I grab her breasts.

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:28.290
And you're the guy who lives next door,
and you have giant testicles!

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:31.330
Cikapasi, that means 
we're not related at all.

00:13:33.830 --> 00:13:37.460
Is he still in Abashiri?

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:38.690
Yes.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.090
"He"?

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:45.280
Inudou Shirosuke,
the Warden of Abashiri Prison.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:49.390
He and I had quite a history 
at Kabato Prison, too.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.300
Speaking of Kabato...

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:55.850
I thought my heart would stop then.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:14:01.380
<b>Tsukigata Kabato Prison</b>

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:00.900
See you next year, sensei.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.010
Have a nice year.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:10.910
Gamushin...

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:22.890
Impossible! Is that you, Hijikata-san?

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:27.720
Inudou-san, you're a terrible man.

00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:32.990
I've spent twenty years here 
as a swordsmanship instructor.

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.930
Why did you never tell me?

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:39.960
<b>Tsukigata Kabato Prison Warden
Inudou Shirosuke</b>

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:39.960
I heard you parted ways 
before the Hakodate War.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:44.190
I have no responsibility to give unrelated 
persons information about prisoners.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:49.990
<b>Long and arduous journey</b>

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:49.990
You lost your brother in the Hakodate War. 
He fought on the new government's side.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:54.060
You may hate him because of that, 
but why hide him from the government?

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:57.950
Or keep him hidden until now, 
instead of executing him?

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:05.160
Did you decide that the worst 
punishment for Hijikata Toshizou

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:07.200
was to steal everything from him,

00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:10.510
and keep him alive in a life without meaning?

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.970
I'm waiting for his light to go out.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:19.750
When the light in his eyes goes out,

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.250
I'll hang him.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.250
Let me see him.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.400
You need to leave.

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:31.010
You're being transferred to 
Abashiri at the start of the year.

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.890
I'll come back then.

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:36.420
Hijikata will be taken to Abashiri.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.860
You're a monster of a warden.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:42.770
But a monster obsessed 
with rules is one thing.

00:15:42.770 --> 00:15:44.890
You're a monster obsessed with revenge.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.600
If you don't let me see him now,
 I'll split your head open!

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.060
S-Sensei!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.960
Get that old geezer out of here!

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:03.140
Toss him out the gates!

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:06.440
Let me go, you damn bureaucrats!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.850
Calm yourself, sensei.

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:11.210
Come with me.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.330
He's in solitary over there.

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:20.360
I can give you 10 minutes 
or so to talk to him.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.800
I owe you one, chief guard.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.340
It's nothing... I'm a swordsman, too.

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.620
Is that you, Gamushin?

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:48.110
I never thought I'd hear 
that name again at my age.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:52.360
It was the fourth year of the Keiou
era when last we met, correct?

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:57.640
I gave up on the Shinsengumi then.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.230
But Hijikata-san,

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:02.950
even if I had my disagreements 
with Kondou-san,

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:07.580
I did everything I did for the 
Shinsengumi because of you.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.770
What's gotten into you, Nagakura Shinpachi?

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:13.010
Age has softened you, I see.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:17.390
If you hadn't protected me from Kondou-san,

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.520
I would've been forced to 
commit seppuku so many times.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.820
You liked the ladies a little too much.

00:17:23.820 --> 00:17:27.810
You're the one who taught me that bad habit!

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.440
We both did a lot of stupid things.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:35.280
We loved fighting with swords, wandering, 
and women more than anyone else.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:37.700
We were a lot alike.

00:17:38.490 --> 00:17:45.290
Your nickname was "Baragaki," 
"a kid as violent as a thorn."

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.290
What a stupid name.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.770
It's a cooler name than "Gamushin," 
or "reckless Shinpachi."

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:54.420
You were stupid and ill-tempered,

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.940
but when you swung your sword, 
it was a thing of beauty.

00:17:56.940 --> 00:17:59.140
And beautiful things should be left alive.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:02.280
When we had that last fight 
before we parted ways,

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:06.890
was that you trying to keep me 
from following you to your death?

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.730
I've spent many nights asking myself that.

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:16.040
If that was the last thing 
all of you did for me...

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:19.860
Am I wrong, Hijikata-san?

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:25.590
You are. I just didn't like 
you because you were an idiot.

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:39.560
Hey, Asirpa-san, are you sure we 
didn't see Hijikata somewhere?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.080
I'm sure I've seen that face before.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.530
Oh, it's just an Ogata.

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:00.490
<b>Ashibetsu</b>

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:04.490
Going to Yuubari gave us important information.
There are fake tattoos out there.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.120
That was a big miscalculation 
on Lt. Tsurumi's part.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:11.420
He probably didn't expect 
us to find out so soon.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:14.090
I'm sorry...

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:16.370
They escaped.

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:19.110
<b>Otaru</b>

00:19:16.370 --> 00:19:22.610
It's fine. It doesn't matter if 
they know the fakes exist or not.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:26.430
I only wanted one thing. Chaos.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:32.670
As long as we can get the 
real ones little by little,

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:35.130
that's all we need.

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:41.530
Don't you think it'll be fun to watch them 
run around helplessly, Lt. Tsukishima?

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.950
Yes, sir.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:49.930
Without a way to tell which ones are fakes,

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:53.040
gathering the skins won't 
help us crack the code.

00:19:53.350 --> 00:19:56.020
There may be no way to tell at all.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:00.210
That would be a real shame.

00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:03.930
We'll have to rely on this man.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:06.680
Me?

00:20:07.090 --> 00:20:10.940
I never thought this useless 
idiot would be our last hope.

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:15.990
The fastest way forward is to talk to 
Nopperabo in Abashiri Prison directly.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.940
Escape King, it's up to you to get us in.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:21.320
I gotta piss!

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:24.390
Shiraishi...

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.150
Sugimoto, you're here!

00:20:30.150 --> 00:20:31.850
How'd you find us?

00:20:31.850 --> 00:20:34.400
Forget that. We need to talk.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.400
Come with me.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:39.490
Where's everybody else?

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.380
I remembered.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:43.460
Remembered what?

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:49.060
After Henmi Kazuo died, we met a 
weird guy at the longhouse, remember?

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:52.060
That was Hijikata Toshizou. I'm sure of it.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:57.690
So you were working with him then?

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.190
You were passing him information 
about us the whole time?

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:04.650
N-No! I was drunk at the longhouse...

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:06.660
You're still going to lie to me?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.080
If you had told the truth, 
I would've forgiven you!

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:26.260
Sugimoto!

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:28.530
Don't—

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.280
<i>Oh, no...</i>

00:21:39.280 --> 00:21:40.440
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.350
<i>I'm scared shitless now!</i>

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:45.240
<i>The gold won't matter if he kills me first!</i>

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:00.960
You... You're Shiraishi, right?

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
The Great Plan to Infiltrate the Asahikawa 7th Division!!</b>

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:39.990
Next Time: "The Great Plan to Infiltrate 
The Asahikawa 7th Division!"
